# Nuxt project conventions (naming + structure)

**Copy this rule into each client project’s `.cursor/rules/`** so generated code matches your team conventions. In that project, keep a `conventions.md` or `docs/conventions.md` (from dotclaude’s `docs/conventions.md`) as the single source of truth.

## Naming (strict)

- **Variables, functions, composables:** lowerCamelCase — e.g. `firstName`, `heroTitleClasses`, `isCompactHeaderVisible`.
- **TypeScript/JS classes, types, interfaces:** PascalCase — e.g. `ArticleItem`, `MicroCmsArticle`.
- **Vue component names in template:** PascalCase — e.g. `<VisionSection />`, `<LocaleSwitcher />`.
- **File names:** kebab-case — e.g. `intro.client.vue`, `locale-switcher.vue`, `use-article-helpers.ts`.
- **Folder names:** lowercase, kebab-case — e.g. `content`, `layout`, `locale-switcher`.
- **Component files:** Prefer kebab-case (e.g. `vision-section.vue`); Nuxt auto-imports as PascalCase.
- **CSS class names in HTML:** Tailwind utilities or kebab-case for custom classes; TS/JS class names stay PascalCase.

## Structure

- **app:** `components/` (by domain: about, card, content, layout, news, ui, …), `composables/`, `layouts/`, `pages/`, `plugins/`, `assets/css/`, `data/`, `constants/`.
- **server:** `api/`, `middleware/`.
- **shared:** `types/`, `utils/`, `stores/`.
- **i18n:** Only when the project uses i18n: `i18n/locales/`.

When generating or refactoring code, follow the project’s **conventions.md** (or **docs/conventions.md**) for full folder layout, stack, and per-project options (i18n, CSS, GSAP).
